# Fuse Box - trying the box with your own Meta Model API key
#
# A provisioned Fuse Box does not need this file: it reaches the cloud
# through the owner's gateway with a per-device token (see the README's
# "Configuration & secrets"). This file is for running a box with your
# own key instead - for example, while evaluating the project.
#
# 1. Copy this file to .env and paste your key after the equals sign.
# 2. Run the installer from this folder:  sudo bash install.sh
#    The installer stores the key on the box at
#    ~/.config/cosmo-voice/meta_api_key with owner-only permissions
#    (0600). An existing key file on the box is left alone.
# 3. You can delete .env afterwards - the box keeps its own copy.
#
# Never commit a filled-in .env.

META_API_KEY=
